BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir The Var//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:The Var — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cade — Toulon’s thick chickpea-flour galette\, baked over wood in a copper pan and eaten hot from paper.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KAHD. The one dish Toulon calls wholly its own\; it is gone by lunch. Best: La Cade à Dédé’s carts at the Place Louis Blanc end of the Cours Lafayette\, Toulon — mornings\, not Monday
LOCATION:La Cade à Dédé’s carts at the Place Louis Blanc end of the Cours Lafayette\, Toulon — mornings\, not Monday
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+Louis+Blanc+Toulon+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Chichi frégi — A sugared ring of chickpea-and-wheat dough\, fried to order.
DESCRIPTION:Say: shee-SHEE fray-ZHEE. Beach and fairground food that Toulon and Marseille both claim. Best: The kiosks of Toulon’s seafront and fairgrounds — no single stall re-confirmed this autumn
LOCATION:The kiosks of Toulon’s seafront and fairgrounds — no single stall re-confirmed this autumn
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Plages+du+Mourillon+Toulon+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tarte tropézienne — A sugar-crusted brioche filled with two creams.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tart tro-pay-ZYEN. Named\, the story goes\, by Bardot on a film set in 1955. Best: La Tarte Tropézienne\, the house Alexandre Micka founded\, Saint-Tropez
LOCATION:La Tarte Tropézienne\, the house Alexandre Micka founded\, Saint-Tropez
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Tarte+Trop%C3%A9zienne+Saint-Tropez+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Grand aïoli — Garlic emulsion with salt cod\, boiled vegetables and eggs\, shared on a Friday.
DESCRIPTION:Say: grahn eye-OH-lee. Provence stops mid-week for it\; eat it once the old way. Best: Le Pont d’Or\, Barjols — Friday lunch\, book ahead
LOCATION:Le Pont d’Or\, Barjols — Friday lunch\, book ahead
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Pont+d%27Or+Barjols+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Daube provençale — Beef or boar braised for hours in red wine with orange peel.
DESCRIPTION:Say: dohb pro-vahn-SAL. Carters’ food of the hills\, best in the chestnut months. Best: La Petite Fontaine\, Collobrières — the boar daube with chestnuts and ceps\; not re-confirmed this autumn\, so call
LOCATION:La Petite Fontaine\, Collobrières — the boar daube with chestnuts and ceps\; not re-confirmed this autumn\, so call
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Petite+Fontaine+Collobrieres+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Soupe de poissons de roche — Rockfish simmered and strained into a rust-coloured broth\, with rouille and croutons.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soop de pwa-SON de rosh. What the coast actually eats when it is not eating bouillabaisse. Best: Hôtel La Ponche\, Saint-Tropez — on the terrace over the gulf
LOCATION:Hôtel La Ponche\, Saint-Tropez — on the terrace over the gulf
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hotel+La+Ponche+Saint-Tropez+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Rouget poached in seawater — Red mullet cooked in seawater\, with crushed tomato and citrus.
DESCRIPTION:Say: roo-ZHAY. Two stars’ worth of the sea without butter: Éric Canino’s signature. Best: La Voile\, La Réserve Ramatuelle — seasonal\, May to October\; book ahead
LOCATION:La Voile\, La Réserve Ramatuelle — seasonal\, May to October\; book ahead
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Reserve+Ramatuelle+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Panier de crudités — A whole basket of raw garden vegetables with eggs and a dip.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pan-YAY de krew-dee-TAY. The plate that has fed Pampelonne since 1955\, from the family’s own farm. Best: Club 55\, Pampelonne — seasonal\, March to 1 November 2026
LOCATION:Club 55\, Pampelonne — seasonal\, March to 1 November 2026
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Club+55+Ramatuelle+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Grilled langouste — Spiny lobster split and grilled\, brought to the table to share.
DESCRIPTION:Say: lahn-GOOST. The island’s great plate\, eaten under the pines after a ferry and a shuttle. Best: Le Mas du Langoustier\, Porquerolles — seasonal\, late April to late September
LOCATION:Le Mas du Langoustier\, Porquerolles — seasonal\, late April to late September
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Mas+du+Langoustier+Porquerolles+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Black truffle — Tuber melanosporum\, the winter truffle of the Haut-Var oak woods.
DESCRIPTION:Say: truff NWAHR. Sold by the gram on Thursday mornings in winter\, checked under the nose. Best: The Aups truffle market\, Place Mistral — Thursday mornings from late November
LOCATION:The Aups truffle market\, Place Mistral — Thursday mornings from late November
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+Mistral+Aups+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Marrons glacés — Whole chestnuts candied slowly in syrup\; and the crème de marrons\, the jar you carry home.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ma-RON gla-SAY. The Maures’ chestnut\, turned into sugar in the village that grows it. Best: Confiserie Azuréenne\, Collobrières
LOCATION:Confiserie Azuréenne\, Collobrières
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Confiserie+Azureenne+Collobrieres+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Figue de Solliès — The near-black Bourjassotte fig\, the only fig in France with an AOP.
DESCRIPTION:Say: feeg de sol-YES. Sold dead-ripe from late August into October\, and never travels well. Best: The growers of Solliès-Pont and the Gapeau valley — in the larder
LOCATION:The growers of Solliès-Pont and the Gapeau valley — in the larder
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sollies-Pont+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tapenade — Olives\, capers and anchovy pounded with oil\, on bread at the apéro.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ta-pe-NAD. The name comes from the Provençal for the caper. Best: The olive stalls of the Cours Lafayette\, Toulon — mornings\, not Monday
LOCATION:The olive stalls of the Cours Lafayette\, Toulon — mornings\, not Monday
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cours+Lafayette+Toulon+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bandol rouge — At least half Mourvèdre\, long in wood\, built to age for decades.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ban-DOL roozh. The Var’s great wine\, and still a fraction of a comparable Burgundy. Best: Domaine de Terrebrune\, Ollioules — at the cellar door\, Monday to Saturday
LOCATION:Domaine de Terrebrune\, Ollioules — at the cellar door\, Monday to Saturday
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+de+Terrebrune+Ollioules+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bandol rosé — A darker\, structured rosé with Mourvèdre in it\, made for fish soup and aïoli.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ban-DOL ro-ZAY. The one Provence pink worth keeping a year. Best: Maison des Vins de Bandol\, chemin de la Ferrage\, Le Castellet — the appellation’s own counter
LOCATION:Maison des Vins de Bandol\, chemin de la Ferrage\, Le Castellet — the appellation’s own counter
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Maison+des+Vins+de+Bandol+Le+Castellet+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Côtes de Provence rosé — Pale\, dry Grenache-Cinsault pink\, drunk young and cold.
DESCRIPTION:Say: koht de pro-VAHNS ro-ZAY. The apéro of the whole coast\; buy it at estate prices\, not beach-club ones. Best: Maison des Vins Côtes de Provence\, Les Arcs-sur-Argens
LOCATION:Maison des Vins Côtes de Provence\, Les Arcs-sur-Argens
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Maison+des+Vins+Cotes+de+Provence+Les+Arcs+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:var-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pastis — Anise spirit with five parts cold water\, poured at six.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pas-TEESS. Marseille’s drink\, and the hour the whole coast keeps. Best: Sénéquier\, on the quay at Saint-Tropez — or any port café at six
LOCATION:Sénéquier\, on the quay at Saint-Tropez — or any port café at six
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Senequier+Saint-Tropez+Var+France
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
